# Livelock kind A fix, folded into darlingserver-diag-ring-sigexc-events.patch (the last patch; darlingserver-suspend-coalesce-inflight.patch is the unlisted standalone copy, equal to the fold-in minus the ring-patch part). A suspend signal is in the handler mask, so the next suspend stayed pending and re-entered the handler right after sigreturn, before the worker ran user code (progress=0). While a suspend signal's handler is in flight no further signal is sent (ring kind 6); the handler parks at thread_suspended or at interrupt_exit (kind 7). The 25 ms watchdog (kind 14) re-sends a lost signal: it is a workaround for the host losing signal 65 (about 1 in 125 rounds on debug), the root cause is not found. Checked on one set: busy info worker stages 80->188, 1500/1500 rounds (750 signalled + 750 coalesced); busy debug stages 26->142, 1500/1500; idle with the clock patches progress=218; sig-reentry 5/5 with and 5/5 without the clock patches.
